{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-stream-solving", "file": "references/session-review-task-dabb45d0.md", "content": "# Session review: demo discipline in a dense grid

The test scene contained many striking shapes and isolated pixels. Three requested demonstrations showed almost entirely unchanged grids; their only edits were localized recolorings: in demo 1, two adjacent 4s became 9s; in demo 2, a three-cell 9 motif became 0s; in demo 3, one 8 became 9. This contradicts interpreting the large motifs as an evident stamp operation. The examples do not establish a reliable selection rule for the test, so do not infer one from appearance alone.

Practical lesson: after each demo, enumerate exact changed cells and candidate unchanged structures immediately. If changes are tiny amid a crowded canvas, compare local object attributes, isolated markers, and relative position across examples; request further demos only to distinguish explicit hypotheses. Avoid spending successive demo requests without stating what uncertainty each one resolves. Preserve the protocol that the final response is exactly one JSON action object.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1792484434/attempts/a51726d22484491ca3bb302d2d403d60/system/state/hermes/skills/puzzle-solving/continual-arc-stream-solving/references/session-review-task-dabb45d0.md"}

